# RAK Hotspot Miner V2: Raspberry Pi 4 + RAK Pi HAT concentrator.
# Confirmed on a test unit with hardware/scripts/probe_concentrator.py (2026-10): SX1302/SX1303
# (version register 0x10) on /dev/spidev0.0, reset on GPIO 25, no power-enable pin needed.
# These match NebraLtd/hm-pyhelper ("rak-fl1").
NEON_DEVICE="RAK Hotspot Miner V2"
NEON_SPI=/dev/spidev0.0
# BCM2711 GPIO controller (label pinctrl-bcm2711, address fe200000), line 25.
# GPIO 17 (RAK's usual HAT reset) is NOT the reset on these units.
NEON_RESET_GPIO_CHIP=fe200000
NEON_RESET_GPIO_LINE=25
# Optional: lower the HAL's SPI clock (Hz) if probe_concentrator.py says the default is too fast.
#NEON_SPI_HZ=1000000
# ECC608 secure element (former Helium key): I2C bus 1, address 0x60, slot 0.
NEON_ECC_I2C_BUS=1
